Command: c
Effect : copy characters to clipboard
Modes  : x, x-y, x@y, <string>

Examples:
c 5     - copy 5 characters to clipboard starting at current char. pointer
c 3-10  - copy characters 3 through 10 inclusive to clipboard
c 6@30  - copy 6 characters starting at character 30 to clipboard
c <str> - copy the string <str> to the clipboard.  The string does not have to
          exist within the line.


Note: Opening a new file does not erase the previous contents of the clipboard.
      You can use this to cut and paste between files.  Also see the help on
      strings.
